    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "is it usually just the sediment though? i was reading online that the knocking could be air in the pipes or something. could i maybe just flush the tank myself to see if that fixes the noise? i'm just trying to avoid a massive call out fee if it's something simple.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Sediment buildup is a very common culprit for noise and poor heating, so that's a strong possibility. You might be able to try flushing the tank yourself, which can sometimes clear out gunk that's causing the noise, but be careful when doing so. If the knocking is more of a rhythmic *clunk* and the water is barely warm, it could definitely be a failing element, which is a bigger job than just flushing.\n\nIf you decide to flush, make sure you follow the manufacturer's instructions precisely, and if you see any rust or heavy sludge, it's time to call a plumber before you proceed further. It's better to have a plumber check it out than to accidentally cause a bigger leak while trying to save a few coins.",
      "source": "target",
